# Publish & live deploy (Loot & Lasers)

## “Commit and push” = fully agent-driven

When the user says **commit and push** (or equivalent), the agent must do **all** of the following **without asking the user to click anything**:

1. **Commit locally** per `git-commit-convention.mdc` (milestone commits; no secrets).
2. **Push to the GitHub remote** that GitHub Desktop tracks (`origin`, usually `main`).  
   - GitHub Desktop is not a separate repo — it syncs this same `origin`.  
   - The agent performs the push (typically `git push -u origin HEAD` / `git push origin main`) using the machine’s stored credentials / Git Credential Manager (same store Desktop uses).  
   - Do **not** tell the user to press Push origin. Do **not** leave push as a manual step.  
   - If push fails for auth, fix or report the credential error; do not silently skip.
3. **Deploy Hetzner Node API** — run `scripts/deploy-hetzner-node-api.ps1` from the local checkout (SSH identity typically `C:\Users\Caide\Desktop\Stuff\Loot and lasers\SSH\Farts`).
4. **Deploy / reload Nakama** on staging — keep modules current and recreate/reload the Nakama service as needed (no game-data wipe). See `docs/STAGING_NAKAMA.md` / host compose when there is no dedicated script.
5. **Never** build a Windows installer / Godot export unless the user **explicitly** asks for one.

## Targets

| Target | On “commit and push” | Who |
|--------|----------------------|-----|
| **GitHub remote** (Desktop’s repo) | Yes — push | Agent |
| **Hetzner Node API** | Yes — deploy | Agent |
| **Nakama** | Yes — reload/deploy | Agent |
| **Godot installer** | Only if asked | Agent when requested |

## Notes

- Prefer non-interactive push (`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` where helpful) so Credential Manager can use saved creds without a cancelled GUI dialog.
- Hetzner/Nakama deploy does not update installed desktop clients (needs a new installer when requested).
